# Enum over StringName

Prefer **`enum`** (usually on `BattleEnums`) over **`StringName`** for identifiers that are a known, closed set.

## Prefer enum when

- Values are fixed and few (resource types, presentation kinds, categories, teams)
- Inspector should show a dropdown
- Typos should fail at edit/compile time
- Call sites compare against a finite list (`STAMINA`, `MANA`, …)

```gdscript
# ❌ BAD — open stringly typed set
@export var resource_id: StringName = &""
execution["presentation"] = &"attack"

# ✅ GOOD
@export var resource_id: BattleEnums.UnitResource = BattleEnums.UnitResource.NONE
execution["presentation"] = BattleEnums.Presentation.ATTACK
```

## StringName is OK when

- Identity is **data-driven / open-ended** (ability `id` like `&"warrior_basic_attack"` — new content without code changes)
- Interop with Godot APIs that expect `StringName` (signals, input actions, node names)
- Keys in heterogeneous dictionaries where an enum would be forced/awkward

If unsure, default to **enum**. Only use `StringName` when you can name one of the reasons above.
